{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/458430-goblin-fruits-fairy-meat-and-other-eldritch-delicacies","id":458430,"title":"Goblin Fruits, Fairy Meat and other Eldritch Delicacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-26T16:03:19-07:00","id":458430,"title":"Goblin Fruits, Fairy Meat and other Eldritch Delicacies","content":"I find the Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue (or Knights de Cusine, or Gastrognomes, if you want to shorten it) from <i>Lords of Summer</i> to be a highly interesting and unique Entitlement, and I was wondering if anyone out there has ever made use of them in their games?<br /> <br /> In particular, I'd love to get ideas to spitball the various sorts of strange ingredients - and stranger dishes - that a Knight could potentially track down or create.<br /> <br /> On a related topic; a character I have planned for a future chronicle is essentially a Knight &quot;procurer&quot;. He's interested in the cooking, but his specialty is providing ingredients. He's a hunter and forager, and even a Hedge-side farmer, specialising in acquiring all of the ingredients he could possibly need for future dishes, and in trading these ingredients to other Knights or even other changelings (since some of them are Goblin Fruits in their own right). Would you consider this character to be a fitting member of the Entitlement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T12:27:51-07:00","id":459254,"title":"","content":"If he meets the requirements for the Entitlement, I see no reason why he wouldn't. The ability to forage/gather is a fundamental part of the Order, as shown in the bonuses the members receive. If he's just more focused on that than the actual art of cooking, that's cool. His dishes just rely more on the quality of ingredients than on fancy chef-work.<br /> <br /> Edit: Try going to any professional butcher, fishmonger, fresh food market, etc. Ask the person in charge for recommendations on how to cook a product. If they know their stuff, they'll give you good advice. People who produce and sell food-stuffs make it their business to know how it's prepared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","user":"Birnam","date":". 03-27-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T13:09:22-07:00","id":459309,"title":"","content":"Thanks; I thought it made sense, fresh-quality is so very important for foodstuffs, and producers are also typically interested in preparing it, I was just a little worried that it might not mesh up well with the theme.<br /> <br /> Now I just need a suitable seeming/kith for him... I'm currently leaning towards making him a Murdermummer (Fairest Seeming, Dual-Kithed Dancer/Razorhand) who took up the role of a Knight de Cuisine to find a way to both be something more than a beautiful butcher and to work off his ingrained need to track and kill. He whets his bloodthirst on hedgebeasts and goblins, and the end result of his art is the food he creates. Does nicely for substituting for his more cannibalistic impulses, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}